From 0e0839dec3a908a228913cbe435b71641e2beafa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:16:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/37] batch: more than 8 slots with a layer split (8 rows per
 pipeline group), hand-off sized per slot

Measured on 4x RTX 3090 (UD-IQ4_XS): 16 and 32 slots decode bit-identical to solo
(tools/batch_test16.py / batch_test32.py); 16 slots 603 tok/s batch decode vs 345 with 8.

Rebased on 0.1.42: the stages' batch row check (batch_rows_error, upstream 48f2c47d) bounds
hbase + S by the hand-off rows; set_handoff_rows passes the per-slot size there (only above 8 slots).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
